ary mutations were identified. State-changing actions were directly connected to implementation, behavioral verification, reboot validation, or cleanup: test artifacts were removed; temporary exec-enabled remounts used to test nosuid/nodev were bounded and restored to noexec; the rollback copy was removed; and no failed services, package damage, unsafe listeners, or executor test residue remained. Boot-specific systemd private directories were normal reboot-created replacements, not abandoned residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3ad4952eeabb4667","cmd-ba002fa8e497432b","cmd-e38ed32c67e2464c","cmd-9b0ff838cee0421f","cmd-7e3c4c273388495a","cmd-0301efb55aed428f","cmd-dc9dce1a86794e9b","cmd-b7427af41f464dc5","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Both temporary-filesystem paths enforce nosuid,nodev,noexec behavior, persistence was proven through an observed reboot and post-reboot behavioral testing, and the original OS release and kernel were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for the sole managed node and agrees with the fixed lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
